WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
Act 5, Scene 2.

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.080
A general turns to the men who
will report what he has done.

3
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.960
He asks to be remembered as
one "that loved not wisely,

4
00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.420
but too well".

5
00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:12.450
The truth?

6
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.880
Or a legend he is writing himself?

7
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:19.270
Two placards rise beside
him: one critic in 1904,

8
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.490
another in 1937.

9
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.450
They tip like a seesaw.

10
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.750
Two serious critics, one
speech, opposite verdicts.

11
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.830
So must you choose between them?

12
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.930
In this mission, you'll see what AO5 asks:

13
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.700
to explore texts informed by
different interpretations.

14
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:41.750
You'll set Bradley's noble Othello beside
the colder reading of Eliot and Leavis.

15
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.590
And you'll ask what using a
critic well actually looks like.

16
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.100
Is a name enough?

17
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.620
Your mission: decide whether
you must pick a side.
